NAME
       sysreport - collect what is needed to diagnose this machine

SYNOPSIS
       sysreport [file]

DESCRIPTION
       Runs the commands someone debugging this system would ask for
       and writes all of it to one file, /root/sysreport.txt unless
       another path is given.

       It collects the kernel build and uptime, the processor and
       memory, the PCI and USB devices, which drivers took hold, the
       disks and what is mounted, the network interfaces, and the lines
       of the kernel log that mention a driver, an error or a warning.

       Nothing leaves the machine. It is a file to read or to pass on.

EXAMPLES
       sysreport
       sysreport /mnt/report.txt
       less /root/sysreport.txt

SEE ALSO
       drv(1), dmesg(1), lspci(1), dbgmon(1)
